@*
    The dashboard: progress across projects and repositories, derived from the
    signal stream the other contexts emit.

    It is empty on purpose, and the wording is careful for a reason. A Dashboard
    in this context is a derived view, not a stored one — Monitoring's only
    aggregate is the Progress Signal, and rollups are computed from the stream
    each time they are read. So nothing here says saved, kept or configured: with
    no signals collected there is nothing to derive, which is a different
    statement from an empty dashboard someone once set up.

    The shell decides *whether* there is a dashboard — the feature flag and the
    header toggle stay there — and this decides what is in one. The ✕ only reports
    that it was pressed; what that closes is the shell's business.
*@

<section @key=@("dashboard-pane") class="dashboard-panel" id="dashboard-pane" aria-labelledby="dashboard-title" data-testid="dashboard-panel">
    <header class="dashboard-panel__header">
        <div>
            <p class="dashboard-panel__eyebrow">Monitoring</p>
            <h2 id="dashboard-title" class="dashboard-panel__title">Dashboard</h2>
            <p class="dashboard-panel__subtitle">Progress across projects and repositories, derived from the signal stream.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dashboard-panel__header-actions">
            <IconButton AriaLabel="Close dashboard" CssClass="btn--ghost" OnClick="() => OnClose.InvokeAsync()">✕</IconButton>
        </div>
    </header>

    <div class="dashboard-panel__content" id="dashboard-content">
        <EmptyState TestId="dashboard-empty-state"
                    Title="No signals yet"
                    Description="No progress signals have been collected, so there is nothing to derive a view from. Once the other contexts start reporting, their progress is summarised here." />
    </div>
</section>

@code {
    /// <summary>Raised when somebody dismisses the dashboard. Whether that
    /// returns to the workspace, opens something else or does nothing is the
    /// shell's decision — the pane only reports that the ✕ was pressed.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnClose { get; set; }
}
